% Origin: test/unit/ssphot.sis
% Port Note: uses rank-polymorphic array_dv (flat dope-vector) instead of unit ragged array (array_dv[array_dv[...]]).
%
% SSPHOT_TRACK -- the particle tracking loop.  This is the construct that made
% ssphot uncompilable, and the reason it was picked as the benchmark to port.
%
% Two nested sequential loops.  The inner one walks the current particle list,
% decides each photon's fate, and emits ncopies copies of it -- 0 if killed or
% absorbed or escaped, 1 if it continues, n if it split.  Those variable-length
% pieces are glued together with
%
%     returns value of catenate tplist
%
% on a FOR-INITIAL, which was rejected outright until 34a02f8:
%
%     for-initial reduction: catenate is not supported in a sequential loop yet
%
% and this is the only program in the whole corpus that asks for it.  Nothing
% else could be sequential here: the loop threads an RNG seed, so iteration i
% cannot start before i-1 finishes, and the number of particles emitted is
% data-dependent.  It is a genuine recurrence producing ragged output -- the
% one shape a forall cannot express.
%
% The outer loop then re-runs on whatever the inner one produced, until the list
% empties.  Splitting can make it grow, so termination is a property of the
% physics (killed and absorbed particles outnumber splits) rather than of a
% trip count -- which is exactly why the outer `while array_size(plist) > 0` has
% no derivable bound either, and needed e55d31b.
%
% NOT PORTED HERE: DetDistToBound, the ray/cell intersection that computes how
% far a photon travels before hitting a zone boundary.  It is independent of
% this loop's structure -- the transport does not care how dbound was obtained,
% only what it is -- so it arrives as a per-zone table alongside the zone
% increments.  Substituting a table keeps the loop, the recurrence and the
% catenate exactly as the original writes them; it does not stand in for the
% geometry, which is still to do.
%
% The 13 tallies are carried as they are in the original: the inner loop SUMS
% them across the particle list, and the outer loop sums those per-pass totals.
% wrr and the kill counters exist so that weight discarded by roulette is booked
% out rather than silently lost -- see ssphot_move_dv, including the split
% branch whose bookkeeping does not balance.
%
% Registered in the dv e2e suite (group SSPHOT_TRACK_DV).  It was BLOCKED for a
% long time on what looked like an INIT positional contract: the INIT -> LoopB
% carry seeds came out SCRAMBLED, every carry taking a different carry's initial
% value, and the emitted C did not compile --
%
%     (v_LoopB_..._I      = v_INIT_..._SEEDA);
%     (v_LoopB_..._SEEDA  = v_INIT_..._TPLIST);
%     error: assigning to 'double' from incompatible type 'sisal_array_t'
%
% The real cause was NAME SHADOWING, not positional arithmetic.  The thirteen
% tallies are declared in BOTH the outer and the inner `initial` clause -- as
% the original source writes them -- so each was a name shared between an
% enclosing and a nested for-initial.  A name rebound in an `initial` clause
% kept its stale boundary import, so carry detection classified it as a capture
% and built no MERGE pair; the loop then had fewer carry slots than INIT
% exported and the positional derivation read the wrong window.  Fixed by
% recording provenance in the symtab (`inherited`) and by clearing a carry's
% BODY/TEST input port by destination rather than by edge identity.
%
% Expected values come from a reference implementation of the same algorithm in
% C, in the harness -- not from literals.  Cross-checked against OSC 13.0.3
% (~/work/oldsisal): the Sisal, the C reference and OSC agree on the seed, both
% tally arrays and ntrac for all six parameter sets.
%
% STILL NOT PORTED: DetDistToBound, the ray/cell intersection that computes how
% far a photon travels before hitting a zone boundary.  It arrives here as a
% per-zone table, which keeps the loop, the recurrence and the catenate exactly
% as the original writes them but does not stand in for the geometry.

define Main

type particletype = record [ u, v, w, x, y, z, age, newgt : double;
                             id, ir : integer ];
type scattrec     = record [ sigtot, sig, scrat : double ];
type Particles    = array_dv [particletype];
type Doubles      = array_dv [double];
type Ints         = array_dv [integer];

function Random (r : double returns double)
   let factor := 41475557.0d0;  rp := r * factor
   in  rp - double_real(trunc(rp))
   end let
end function

function RRWeights (seed, wmin : double; p : particletype
                    returns double, particletype, double, integer,
                            integer, integer)
   if (p.newgt < wmin) then
      let newseed := Random(seed)
      in
         if (newseed < p.newgt) then
            newseed, p replace [newgt : 1.0d0], 1.0d0 - p.newgt, 0, 0, 1
         else
            newseed, p, -p.newgt, 1, 0, 0
         end if
      end let
   elseif (p.newgt < (1.0d0 / wmin)) then
      seed, p, 0.0d0, 0, 0, 1
   else
      let ir0 := integer(trunc(p.newgt));  ir1 := ir0 - 1
      in
         if (ir1 <= 0) then
            seed, p, 0.0d0, 0, 0, 1
         else
            seed, p replace [newgt : p.newgt / (double_real(ir1) + 1.0d0)],
            0.0d0, 0, ir1, ir1 + 1
         end if
      end let
   end if
end function

function RRImportances (seed : double; idold : integer; ximp : Doubles;
                        p : particletype
                        returns double, particletype, double, integer,
                                integer, integer)
   if (ximp[p.id] = ximp[idold]) then
      seed, p, 0.0d0, 0, 0, 1
   else
      let
         r    := ximp[p.id] / ximp[idold];
         zeta := Random(seed);
         ir1  := integer(trunc(r));
         r1   := double_real(ir1);
         ir0  := ir1 - 1;
         r0   := r - r1
      in
         if ((r < 1.0d0) & (zeta < r0)) then
            let rinv := 1.0d0 / r
            in  zeta, p replace [newgt : p.newgt * rinv],
                p.newgt * (rinv - 1.0d0), 0, 0, 1
            end let
         elseif (r < 1.0d0) then
            zeta, p, -p.newgt, 1, 0, 0
         elseif (zeta < r0) then
            zeta, p replace [newgt : p.newgt / (r1 + 1.0d0)], 0.0d0, 0, ir1, ir1 + 1
         elseif (ir0 <= 0) then
            zeta, p, 0.0d0, 0, 0, 1
         else
            zeta, p replace [newgt : p.newgt / (r1 + 1.0d0)], 0.0d0, 0, ir0, ir0 + 1
         end if
      end let
   end if
end function

function Move (seed : double; p : particletype;
               incr, nzones, mid, irr : integer;
               dbound : double; ximp : Doubles; wcut : double
               returns double, particletype, double, integer, integer,
                       integer, integer, double)
   let
      idold := p.id;
      newid := p.id + incr
   in
      if (newid > nzones) then
         seed, p, 0.0d0, 0, 0, 0, 1, p.newgt
      else
         let
            newp := p replace [ x   : p.x + p.u * dbound;
                                y   : p.y + p.v * dbound;
                                z   : p.z + p.w * dbound;
                                age : p.age + dbound * 3.3356349d-11;
                                id  : newid;
                                ir  : mid ]
         in
            if (irr = 0) then
               seed, newp, 0.0d0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0.0d0
            elseif (irr = 1) then
               RRImportances(seed, idold, ximp, newp), 0, 0.0d0
            else
               RRWeights(seed, wcut, newp), 0, 0.0d0
            end if
         end let
      end if
   end let
end function

% Thomson scattering: sample a deflection cosine from the tabulated
% distribution and rotate the direction cosines about it
function Thom (seed : double; p : particletype
               returns double, particletype)
   let
      % the source's 128-point table is a cosine ramp; regenerating it keeps the
      % file readable and the sampling identical in shape
      csn := for k in 1, 128
             returns array_dv of cos( (double_real(k - 1) / 128.0d0)
                                      * 3.1415926535897932d0 )
             end for;
      seed1  := Random(seed);
      index  := integer(trunc(seed1 * 128.0d0 + 1.0d0));
      sctang := csn[index];
      seed2  := Random(seed1);
      t3     := 6.2831853d0 * seed2;
      t4     := sqrt(1.0d0 - sctang * sctang);
      t5     := sqrt(1.0d0 - p.w * p.w);
      temp1  := t4 / t5;
      temp2  := sin(t3);
      temp3  := cos(t3);
      temp4  := p.w * temp3
   in
      seed2,
      p replace [ u : p.u * sctang + temp1 * (p.u * temp4 - p.v * temp2);
                  v : p.v * sctang + temp1 * (p.v * temp4 + p.u * temp2);
                  w : p.w * sctang - (t4 * t5) * temp3 ]
   end let
end function

% one photon's fate: lost, moved to a boundary, absorbed, scattered, or censused
function DetParticleFate (seed : double; p : particletype;
                          dbound, tcen, wcut : double;
                          incr, nzones, mid, irr : integer;
                          ximp : Doubles; scatter : scattrec
                          returns double, particletype, double, integer,
                                  integer, integer, integer, double, integer,
                                  double, integer, double, integer, integer,
                                  double)
   if (dbound = 1000.0d0) then                      % lost
      seed, p, 0.0d0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0.0d0, 1, p.newgt, 0, 0.0d0, 0, 0, 0.0d0
   else
      let
         seed1 := Random(seed);
         dist  := -log(seed1) / scatter.sig;        % free path to a collision
         dcen  := (tcen - p.age) * 2.99793d10       % distance to census time
      in
         if ((dbound < dist) & (dbound < dcen)) then
            Move(seed1, p, incr, nzones, mid, irr, dbound, ximp, wcut),
            0, 0.0d0, 0, 0.0d0, 0, 0, 0.0d0
         elseif (dist < dcen) then
            let seed2 := Random(seed1)
            in
               if (seed2 > scatter.scrat) then      % absorbed
                  seed2, p, 0.0d0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0.0d0, 0, 0.0d0, 1, p.newgt,
                  0, 0, 0.0d0
               else                                 % collision: scatter
                  let
                     newp := p replace [ x   : p.x + p.u * dist;
                                         y   : p.y + p.v * dist;
                                         z   : p.z + p.w * dist;
                                         age : p.age + dist * 3.3356349d-11 ];
                     seed3, newnewp := Thom(seed2, newp)
                  in
                     if (irr = 2) then
                        RRWeights(seed3, wcut, newnewp),
                        0, 0.0d0, 0, 0.0d0, 0, 0.0d0, 1, 0, 0.0d0
                     else
                        seed3, newnewp, 0.0d0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0.0d0, 0, 0.0d0,
                        0, 0.0d0, 1, 0, 0.0d0
                     end if
                  end let
               end if
            end let
         else                                       % reached census time
            seed1, p, 0.0d0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0.0d0, 0, 0.0d0, 0, 0.0d0, 0, 1, p.newgt
         end if
      end let
   end if
end function

function TrackParticles (seed : double; p : particletype;
                         tcen, wcut : double;
                         nzones, mid, irr : integer;
                         incrs : Ints; dbounds : Doubles;
                         ximp : Doubles; scatter : scattrec
                         returns double, double, integer, integer, integer,
                                 double, integer, double, integer, double,
                                 integer, integer, double, integer)
   for initial
      plist  := array_dv Particles [1: p];
      seed0  := seed;
      wrr    := 0.0d0;  nrr   := 0;  nsplt := 0;
      nescgp := 0;      enesc := 0.0d0;
      nlost  := 0;      wlost := 0.0d0;
      nabs   := 0;      wabs  := 0.0d0;
      nscat  := 0;      ncen  := 0;  wcen := 0.0d0;
      ntrac  := 0
   while (array_size(plist) > 0)
   repeat
      len   := array_size(old plist);
      ntrac := old ntrac + len;
      seed0, plist, wrr, nrr, nsplt, nescgp, enesc,
        nlost, wlost, nabs, wabs, nscat, ncen, wcen :=
           for initial
              i      := 1;
              seedA  := old seed0;
              tplist := array_dv Particles [];
              wrr    := 0.0d0;  nrr   := 0;  nsplt := 0;
              nescgp := 0;      enesc := 0.0d0;
              nlost  := 0;      wlost := 0.0d0;
              nabs   := 0;      wabs  := 0.0d0;
              nscat  := 0;      ncen  := 0;  wcen := 0.0d0
           while (i <= len)
           repeat
              q  := old plist[old i];
              db := dbounds[q.id];
              seedA, newp, wrr, nrr, nsplt, ncopies, nescgp, enesc,
                nlost, wlost, nabs, wabs, nscat, ncen, wcen :=
                   DetParticleFate(old seedA, q, db, tcen, wcut,
                                   incrs[q.id], nzones, mid, irr, ximp, scatter);
              % 0 copies if it died, 1 if it lives, n if it split
              tplist := for k in 1, ncopies returns array_dv of newp end for;
              i      := old i + 1
           returns
              value of seedA
              value of catenate tplist
              value of sum wrr
              value of sum nrr
              value of sum nsplt
              value of sum nescgp
              value of sum enesc
              value of sum nlost
              value of sum wlost
              value of sum nabs
              value of sum wabs
              value of sum nscat
              value of sum ncen
              value of sum wcen
           end for
   returns
      value of seed0
      value of sum wrr
      value of sum nrr
      value of sum nsplt
      value of sum nescgp
      value of sum enesc
      value of sum nlost
      value of sum wlost
      value of sum nabs
      value of sum wabs
      value of sum nscat
      value of sum ncen
      value of sum wcen
      value of ntrac
   end for
end function

function Main (nzones, mid, irr : integer;
               seed, newgt, tcen, wcut, sig, scrat : double
              returns
               double,    % seed out
               Doubles,   % wrr enesc wlost wabs wcen
               Ints,      % nrr nsplt nescgp nlost nabs nscat ncen ntrac
               integer)   % ntrac again, for readability
   let
      ximp    := array_dv Doubles [1: 1.0d0, 1.0d0, 2.0d0, 2.0d0, 1.0d0];
      % what DetDistToBound would have produced, one per zone
      dbounds := array_dv Doubles [1: 0.5d0, 0.75d0, 1.0d0, 1.25d0, 1000.0d0];
      incrs   := array_dv Ints    [1: 1, 1, 1, 1, 1];
      scatter := record scattrec [ sigtot : 1.0d0; sig : sig; scrat : scrat ];
      p := record particletype [ u : 0.5d0; v : 0.5d0; w : 0.7071067811865476d0;
                                 x : 0.0d0; y : 0.0d0; z : 0.0d0;
                                 age : 0.0d0; newgt : newgt; id : 1; ir : 1 ];
      s1, wrr, nrr, nsplt, nescgp, enesc, nlost, wlost,
        nabs, wabs, nscat, ncen, wcen, ntrac :=
           TrackParticles(seed, p, tcen, wcut, nzones, mid, irr,
                          incrs, dbounds, ximp, scatter)
   in
      s1,
      array_dv Doubles [1: wrr, enesc, wlost, wabs, wcen],
      array_dv Ints [1: nrr, nsplt, nescgp, nlost, nabs, nscat, ncen, ntrac],
      ntrac
   end let
end function
